hived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-02-03T23:48:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T10:11:19Z","closed_at":"2026-03-01T10:10:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115852","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115852.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115852.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This adds a new global `assert_release` keyword which functions the same as `assert`, but runs in all build types, including release.\r\n\r\nThis is particularly useful for avoiding crashes due to malicious data sent using rpcs. Normal `assert` is not useful because the main reason for me to include checks here is not really for myself but mostly for players who are running release builds.\r\n\r\nRelated to https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/502\r\nI'm not sure if this closes the proposal because everyone in the proposal has a different idea of how an `assert` for release builds should work. Currently `assert_all` is exactly the same as `assert` except it runs in release builds as well.\r\n\r\nIf someone has a better name I am open to changing it.\r\n\r\nAnother idea I haven't explored is instead adding an argument to `assert` which defaults to `false` that controls whether it is included in release builds.","closed_by":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https:/